lesson: 233
title: Making teams
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: A volleyball team has 6 players on the court.
explain: To make full teams, share the children into groups of 6; the children who do not fill a group are left over and do not make a team.
explain: 27 children: 27 ÷ 6 is 4 with 3 left over, so 4 full volleyball teams, and 3 children keep score.
vars: a=name c=13..60
answer: (c - c % 6) / 6
exercise: {c} children want to play volleyball. How many full volleyball teams can they make?
exercise: A PE teacher has {c} pupils and makes as many full volleyball teams as possible. How many teams are there?
exercise: At camp, {c} children are put into volleyball teams. The children left over keep score. How many full teams are there?
exercise: How many complete volleyball teams can be made from {c} players?
exercise: {a} sorts {c} classmates into volleyball teams, as many full teams as {a.he} can. How many teams does {a.he} make?
exercise: {c} girls come to the volleyball club. How many full teams can play?
exercise: {c} kids, volleyball, how many full teams can we make
exercise: we got {c+1} — sorry {c} kids for volleyball, how many teams, leftovers can ref
exercise: {c} of us at the park lol. volleyball teams, full ones only. how many
exercise: volleyball after school, {c} kids turned up, oh and 2 parents watching but they're not playing. how many full teams
exercise: {a} reckons every kid gets a team but nah. {c} kids, full volleyball teams only, how many teams
test: Out of {c} pupils, how many full volleyball sides can be formed?
test: {c} children turn up to volleyball practice. Teams must be full. How many teams play?
test: The coach splits {c} players into whole volleyball teams; anyone left waits. How many teams are there?
test: volleyball, {c} kids, full teams how many
test: {c} at practice, gotta be full volleyball teams, rest on the bench. teams?
test: How many volleyball teams, each complete, can a school with {c} keen players put out?
exam: Determine the maximum number of complete volleyball teams that may be constituted from a cohort of {c} pupils.
exam: It is given that {c} participants are available. Ascertain the greatest number of full volleyball teams that can be formed, any remainder being excluded.
exam: Compute the number of complete volleyball teams formed when {c} players are allocated thereto to the greatest extent possible.
exam: Whereas {c.words} children present themselves for volleyball, state the number of teams of full complement which may be assembled.
exercise: {c+2} kids came to volleyball, but 2 were "a bit under the weather" and sat on the bench. The rest make as many full teams of 6 as they can. How many full teams are there?
exercise: {c} of us, coach says the leftovers "support from the sidelines", aka sit on yer backside. how many full volleyball teams
test: The sign-up list was "a little optimistic": it said {c+6} children, but only {c} turned up. How many complete volleyball teams can be made, with the leftover children keeping score?
